{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>And I shall return in peace.</b> From the illnesses that also carry a person away — it is the evil spirit that they of blessed memory mentioned for a blessing." "<b>And HaShem will be to me for Elohim.</b> Then HaShem will be to me as a judge if I do not serve Him with all my might. And the vav functions like in this case in place of 'behold' — that is: I hereby accept upon myself from now that the blessed El, the merciful One, will be to me for Elohim and will deal with me according to the measure of justice."], :book :genesis, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {1 "The phrase וְהַוָּא\"ו כְּמוֹ זֹאת is read as referring to the vav of וְהָיָה serving in an anticipatory/presentative sense ('behold'); 'זֹאת' is taken as pointing to the verse's own usage."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:32:14.187067419Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}